{
  "name": "Score remote job listings against your CV with AI and alert on Telegram",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Score remote job listings against your CV with AI and alert on Telegram\n\nTwice a day this workflow pulls fresh remote jobs from three free sources, keeps the ones matching your keywords, has AI score each against your CV from 0 to 100, and sends only strong matches to Telegram with reasons and skill gaps.\n\n### How it works\n1. The Schedule Trigger runs at 9am and 5pm (the job APIs ask for no more than 4 calls a day).\n2. Jobs are fetched in parallel from the Remotive API, the Remote OK API and the We Work Remotely RSS feed. If one source is down, the others still run.\n3. A Code node normalises the three formats, keeps recent jobs matching your keywords, sorts newest first and caps how many get scored.\n4. Jobs already scored in earlier runs are dropped.\n5. Gemini scores each job against your CV and returns JSON: score, one-line verdict, matching and missing skills, and whether the location works for you.\n6. Jobs at or above your `min_score` are sent to Telegram with a link to the original listing. An optional, disabled Google Sheets node can log them.\n\n### Setup\n1. Paste your CV and preferences into **Set your CV and preferences**, then edit `keywords`, `min_score` and `telegram_chat_id`.\n2. Add a **Google Gemini (PaLM) API** credential (free key from aistudio.google.com).\n3. Add a **Telegram** bot credential from @BotFather and message your bot once.\n4. Optional: enable **Log match to Google Sheets**, put the Sheet ID in **Set your CV and preferences** and add a `Matches` tab.\n5. Activate the workflow.\n\n### Customization\n- Raise `max_jobs_per_run` or add more RSS feeds to the merge.\n\nRemotive and Remote OK ask you to credit them and link to their listing, which the alert does.",
        "height": 960,
        "width": 560
      },
      "id": "0874fa0f-c402-5166-a031-7505e6f2a491",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
